jitCmpOperandAT -- SEQ 376 (Tony, R1 a / R2): a compare's result is its own SSA value, never its operand's jitData. Every
read of an inlined callee's argument follows to ONE node, the caller's operand. Before the cure the first compare
(argument < 0) left its i1 on that node's jitData, the second compare read it, and LLVM aborted the build -- icmp with
an i1 and an i32 operand, exit 134, nothing printed (measured 2026-10-17). Same mechanism as JRS-1 / rsG (seal 168),
where the argument was a literal and the constants folded instead of asserting. Intended: jitted = interpreted,
5/5/7/7 (caA is 7 at run time, neither compare true).
